CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ \[this\] reads the live member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ \[=\] in member reads the live member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ \[this\] modifies the live member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ \[this\] observes the update: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ \[\*this\] snapshots at capture time: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[expr.prim.lambda.capture] / [expr.prim.lambda.closure]: `[this]` and a
capture-default that odr-uses members capture the enclosing object by reference
(member odr-uses denote the live object and may modify it); `[*this]` captures
it by copy (a snapshot at capture time).  Lambda rework Phase E models this as
captures of the odr-used data members -- by reference for `this`/`[=]`/`[&]`, by
copy for `[*this]`.
